[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   step_089: Bipolar morphology audit -- is the boundary single-faced?
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   The injected JFC chain terminates on BOTH poles of the measured axis
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   (steps 052/056), so the underlying structure is axisymmetric in
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   aphelion direction.  The transit channel has so far been scored only
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   against the +axis cap (theta < 60 deg).  If the boundary were a
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   two-sided sheet or a symmetric pair of structures, comets whose
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   aphelia point near the anti-axis (theta > 120 deg, the mirror cap)
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   should carry a second slip lobe of comparable amplitude.  This step
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   measures the full theta profile of the catalogue rotation and the
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   planetary-subtracted proper-time residual, and tests:
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   T1  mirror-cap elevation: median(drot_cat, theta>120) vs the
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   mid-region (60-120) background -- Mann-Whitney + bootstrap bound
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   on any second-lobe amplitude;
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   T2  cap/anti-cap contrast: median(drot_cat, theta<60) vs theta>120
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   -- expected significant if the anomaly is localized to +axis;
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   T3  monotonic decay: Spearman of the residuals against theta over
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   the full range -- a localized single structure decays
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   monotonically, a bipolar structure is non-monotone;
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   T4  sign structure: the mid-region (60-120) residual median and the
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   fraction of positive residuals -- the bins adjoining the cap
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   carry a systematically negative median that a two-lobe reading
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   would not predict;
[2026-09-21 15:02:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 089]   T5  per-catalogue replication of all medians (CODE, Warsaw).
